IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, section 2(2) -- WHEN A SPECIFIED AGE IS DEEMED TO BE REACHED.
--
-- The one substantive rule in the Act's interpretation provisions, and the one every piece that
-- tests an age (60, 65, 18, 21, 25 ...) must go through. Wherever the Act speaks of a person
-- "reaching" an age, the person is deemed to reach it on the FIRST DAY OF THE MONTH AFTER the month
-- of the birthday, except in ten places the subsection lists, where the actual birthday governs.
-- Those ten places are the constructors of `Provision about reaching an age`.
--
-- A piece that tests an age calls `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age
-- on a date for a provision` with the constructor for the provision it is encoding, and with
-- `any other provision` for every provision that is not on the list.
--
-- The date of birth is a DATE. The actual birthday is the date of birth plus the age in years;
-- for a birth on 29 February in a year that has no 29 February the birthday is taken as 28 February
-- (daydate's `add years` clamps). The Interpretation Act is not among the texts this encoding
-- reads, so that is an assumption, not a ruling (NOTES.md, fork register, F2). It matters: the other
-- reading, 1 March, puts the birthday in March and so moves the deemed date a month later, from 1 March
-- to 1 April.

§ `Section 2(2) -- when a specified age is deemed to be reached`

§§ `The provisions where the actual birthday governs`

-- src:85 | (2) For the purposes of any provision of this Act in which reference is made to the reaching by a person of a specified age — other than a reference in paragraph 13(1)(c) or (e) or (1.2)(c), 17(c), 17.1(c), 19(c) or (d) or 44(3)(a), section 70 or subparagraph 72(a)(iii) — the person is deemed to have reached the specified age at the beginning of the month following the month in which the person actually reached that age, and in computing
-- src:86 | (a) any period of months ending with the time when he reached a specified age, the month in which he actually reached that age shall be included; and
-- src:87 | (b) any period of months commencing with the time when he reached a specified age, the month in which he actually reached that age shall not be included.
@ref Act s 2(2), the references it excepts (src:85)
DECLARE `Provision about reaching an age` IS ONE OF
    `paragraph 13(1)(c)`
    `paragraph 13(1)(e)`
    `paragraph 13(1.2)(c)`
    `paragraph 17(c)`
    `paragraph 17.1(c)`
    `paragraph 19(c)`
    `paragraph 19(d)`
    `paragraph 44(3)(a)`
    `section 70`
    `subparagraph 72(a)(iii)`
    `any other provision`

§§ `The actual birthday and the deemed date`

-- Not a provision: the birthday on which a person actually reaches an age, from the date of birth.
GIVEN `date of birth` IS A DATE
      age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date a person actually reaches a specified age` `date of birth` age MEANS
    `add years` `date of birth` age

-- Not a provision: a person's actual age in whole years on a date. Nobody has reached an age
-- before the birthday on which they actually reach it, so the age is the number of years between the
-- dates, less one if this year's birthday has not yet come.
GIVEN `date of birth` IS A DATE
      `on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the actual age of a person in whole years on a date` `date of birth` `on` MEANS
    IF `on` AT LEAST (`add years` `date of birth` ((DATE_YEAR `on`) MINUS (DATE_YEAR `date of birth`)))
    THEN (DATE_YEAR `on`) MINUS (DATE_YEAR `date of birth`)
    ELSE ((DATE_YEAR `on`) MINUS (DATE_YEAR `date of birth`)) MINUS 1

@ref Act s 2(2) (src:85)
GIVEN `date of birth` IS A DATE
      age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2(2) — the date a person is deemed to reach a specified age` `date of birth` age MEANS
    `the month following the month of a date` (`the date a person actually reaches a specified age` `date of birth` age)

@ref Act s 2(2) (src:85)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision about reaching an age`
      `date of birth` IS A DATE
      age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` provision `date of birth` age MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `any other provision` THEN `s 2(2) — the date a person is deemed to reach a specified age` `date of birth` age
    OTHERWISE `the date a person actually reaches a specified age` `date of birth` age

@ref Act s 2(2) (src:85)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision about reaching an age`
      `date of birth` IS A DATE
      age IS A NUMBER
      `on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` provision `date of birth` age `on` MEANS
    `on` AT LEAST (`s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` provision `date of birth` age)

§§ `Periods of months that end or begin with the age`

@ref Act s 2(2)(a) (src:86)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `date of birth` IS A DATE
      age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(2)(a) — a month is counted in a period of months ending with a specified age` month `date of birth` age MEANS
    `the month of a date` month AT MOST (`the month of a date` (`the date a person actually reaches a specified age` `date of birth` age))

@ref Act s 2(2)(b) (src:87)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `date of birth` IS A DATE
      age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(2)(b) — a month is counted in a period of months commencing with a specified age` month `date of birth` age MEANS
    `the month of a date` month AT LEAST (`the month following the month of a date` (`the date a person actually reaches a specified age` `date of birth` age))
